  "judgment": {
    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "All six answers agree mathematically with their own captured worked solutions. q-158559: the square root in the denominator must be strictly positive, so x>-2, with y unrestricted. q-158563: the numerator requires y≥-2 and the denominator requires y≠2x³. q-158438 and q-158569: their polynomial exponents are defined everywhere, and positive-base exponential functions accept every real exponent, so both domains are the entire plane. q-158198: x²-y²≥0 is equivalent to -|x|≤y≤|x|, giving the left and right wedges with solid boundaries, option 1. q-158200: the denominator excludes exactly x=2, giving both sides of a dashed vertical line, option 1. For these last two questions, MA's source images contain annotations; the selected current images depict the same regions without annotations. Their different image paths do not represent mathematical disagreements.",
